[agent:result]                 The values should be booleans indicating the setting.
[agent:result]                 To fully turn off statistics computation pass `statistics_config=False`.
[agent:result]                 Defaults to `None` and will compute only descriptive statistics.
[agent:result]             write_options:
[agent:result]                 Additional options as key/value pairs to pass to the execution engine.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]                 For `spark` engine: Dictionary of read options for Spark.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]                 When using the `python` engine, write_options can contain the following entries:
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]                 - key `use_spark` and value `True` to materialize training dataset with Spark instead of [Hopsworks Feature Query Service][arrowflight-server-with-duckdb].
[agent:result]                 - key `spark` and value an object of type [hsfs.core.job_configuration.JobConfiguration][hsfs.core.job_configuration.JobConfiguration] to configure the Hopsworks Job used to compute the training dataset.
[agent:result]                 - key `wait_for_job` and value `True` or `False` to configure whether or not to the save call should return only after the Hopsworks Job has finished.
[agent:result]                   By default it waits.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]             spine:
[agent:result]                 Spine dataframe with primary key, event time and label column to use for point in time join when fetching features.
[agent:result]                 Defaults to `None` and is only required when feature view was created with spine group in the feature query.
[agent:result]                 It is possible to directly pass a spine group instead of a dataframe to overwrite the left side of the feature join, however, the same features as in the original feature group that is being replaced need to be available in the spine group.
[agent:result]             transformation_context:
[agent:result]                 A dictionary mapping variable names to objects that will be provided as contextual information to the transformation function at runtime.
[agent:result]                 The `context` variable must be explicitly defined as parameters in the transformation function for these to be accessible during execution.
[agent:result]             data_source: The data source specifying the location of the data. Overrides the storage_connector and location arguments when specified.
[agent:result]             tags: Tags to attach to the training dataset for better discoverability.
